# Rocketship BEM and SCSS Conventions

- **BEM block naming**
  - Use `rs` as the global block prefix to avoid clashes, e.g.:
    - `.rs-button`, `.rs-button__icon`, `.rs-button--primary`
    - `.rs-link`, `.rs-link__icon`, `.rs-link--muted`
  - Elements use `__`, modifiers use `--` exactly as in classic BEM.

- **Class responsibilities**
  - Blocks are reusable components (e.g. `rs-button`, `rs-container`).
  - Elements are structural parts of a block (e.g. `rs-button__label`, `rs-card__media`).
  - Modifiers represent visual/behavioral variants (e.g. `rs-button--secondary`, `rs-button--outline`).

- **Tokens**
  - `$rs-tokens` in `styles/mixins/tokens.scss` is the single source of truth. Each token is a plain value, a `(light: …, dark: …)` pair, or an `(alias: other-token)`.
  - `variables.scss` is generated from the map with `rs-token-properties`. Edit values in the map, never in `variables.scss`.
  - Colour pairs compile to `light-dark()`; shadow pairs compile to layered shadows whose inactive mode is transparent, so each mode's shadow keeps its exact shape. Dark mode follows `color-scheme`.
  - Components reference tokens only through `#{rs-token(name)}`, which falls back to the default value. Never hand-write hex, px or rem token fallbacks. Unknown names fail the build.
  - A token's name is its contract. Use it only for the role it states: `*-fg` is text on the matching `*-bg`, `*-accent` is a stroke or fill (3:1), `*-text` is text on page surfaces (4.5:1). A role with no token gets a new one (an alias is fine), with the founder's approval.

- **Variables files (e.g. `variables.scss`)**
  - Must **never** contain class selectors (or any selectors other than `:root` and `@media`).
  - Only define CSS custom properties on `:root` and inside `@media`. Component-specific tokens and class-based overrides belong in the component that owns them.

- **SCSS usage**
  - Prefer SCSS for authoring styles; compile to CSS for consumers.
  - Use SCSS features for maintainability (nesting, variables, mixins), but **CSS custom properties** remain the public API for theming.
  - Component styles must be written directly inside the Astro component in a `<style lang="scss">` block.
  - Do not create separate component `.scss` files when the style belongs to a single component.
  - In component `<style lang="scss">` blocks, import mixins via the barrel only: `@use '../styles/mixins' as *;`. Do not `@use` individual files under `styles/mixins/` (`functions`, `container-query`, etc.) — `styles/mixins.scss` already `@forward`s them. Direct `@use` of a mixin partial is for other Sass files that must avoid the full barrel (e.g. `variables.scss`).
  - An explanatory comment sits above the rule it explains as a Sass doc comment (`///`), the SCSS counterpart of a JSDoc block. Never `/* */` or `/** */`: Sass keeps those in the compiled CSS, so they ship to consumers.
  - Use `media-breakpoint-up` only in Container/layout styles; use container queries for component/typography size changes.
  - Use `to-rem($px)` (from the mixins barrel) for every `font-size` authored in SCSS (design-token `--rs-font-size-*`, component fallbacks, body copy in `base.scss`, etc.), so sizes are defined from px and emitted as `rem`. Typography mixins already use `to-rem()`. Exception: print styles may use `pt` where appropriate.
  - Use `px` for all other dimensional values (including spacing, radii, layout dimensions, container-query thresholds, viewport breakpoints, letter-spacing, underline offsets, and underline thickness).
  - `rem` is for font sizes only. No `em` font sizes; use `font-size: inherit` when an element should follow its context.
  - Always interpolate token calls, `#{rs-token(space-4)}`: Sass does not evaluate functions inside custom property values.

- **Declaration order (per rule block)**
  - **CSS custom properties (`--rs-*`) always first** in the block.
  - Then reset if needed (e.g. `all: unset` for buttons/controls), then `box-sizing` if you reset.
  - Then all other properties (layout, appearance, etc.).

- **CSS variable conventions**
  - All design tokens and component-level variables exposed to users should be named with the `--rs-*` prefix, for example:
    - `--rs-color-bg`, `--rs-color-fg`
    - `--rs-color-accent`, `--rs-color-border`
    - `--rs-font-family-sans`, `--rs-font-size-md`
    - `--rs-space-sm`, `--rs-radius-md`
  - Component-specific variables should still follow the `--rs-*` prefix and clearly indicate scope (e.g. `--rs-button-bg`, `--rs-button-border-radius`).

- **No inline styles for design**
  - Do not use inline `style="..."` attributes for anything related to design or theming.
  - Use classes + `--rs-*` variables instead so themes and consumers can override styles cleanly.

- **Selector style (hardcore BEM)**
  - Every compiled selector is a **single BEM class**, plus pseudo-classes or pseudo-elements on that same class (`:hover`, `:focus-visible`, `::before`).
  - Never descendant, child, sibling or compound-class selectors (`.rs-a .rs-b`, `.rs-a > *`, `.rs-a--x .rs-a__y`). Never tag or ID selectors in components.
  - A modifier changes its elements only by reassigning `--rs-*` variables on the block; elements read those variables. An element styles nested elements the same way: a table row sets variables its cells inherit.
  - Structural pseudo-classes on an element's own class are allowed (`.rs-table__body-row:nth-child(even)`, `:last-child`). Selecting children by tag is not (`tbody tr td`).
  - Parent state a child must react to (e.g. parent hover) uses a style query: the parent sets a custom property and the child uses `@container style(--rs-x-state: value)`.
  - Write elements and modifiers nested under their owning block with `&__element` / `&--modifier`. This is source organisation; it compiles flat.
  - The base class is the default: a default variant has no modifier class or rule, and no class appears in markup without a rule.

- **Component boundaries**
  - A component never sets its own outer margin; whoever places it owns the spacing (Stack, Grid, the page).
  - Components never set `font-family`; they inherit the page's typeface.
  - Inline components (Label) set no `display`; the parent's layout decides whether they are block or inline.
  - Semantic groups (Fieldset) add no box: no background, border, radius or padding. Native chrome is reset, and a consumer who wants a panel composes a Card.
  - Never nest an element under a pseudo-class (`&:disabled { &__legend {} }` compiles to an invalid selector). Parent state is a block variable or a style query.
  - Element classes the consumer applies set `margin: 0`, and set their own `color` when they sit on a component-owned background.
  - The component is the semantic element (Table renders one `<table>`), never a wrapper that `class`, modifiers and hooks cannot reach. Scrolling is a separate primitive (`Scroll`) the placer wraps around it.
  - Density is padding hooks, never a `compact`/`size` prop; static content has no hover state.
  - Use logical properties (`inline-size`, `padding-block-end`, `text-align: start` / `end`).

